<article class="env-definition" id="02QR">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02QR">Definition <span data-tag="02QR">42.8.1</span>.</a> Let $(S, \delta )$ be as in Situation <a href="/tag/02QL" data-tag="02QL">42.7.1</a>. Let $X$ be locally of finite type over $S$. Let $k \in \mathbf{Z}$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
A <em>cycle on $X$</em> is a formal sum 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \alpha = \sum n_ Z [Z]  \]
</div>
<p>
 where the sum is over integral closed subschemes $Z \subset X$, each $n_ Z \in \mathbf{Z}$, and the collection $\{ Z; n_ Z \not= 0\} $ is locally finite (Topology, Definition <a href="/tag/0BDS" data-tag="0BDS">5.28.4</a>). 
</p>
</li><li><p>
A <em>$k$-cycle</em> on $X$ is a cycle 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \alpha = \sum n_ Z [Z]  \]
</div>
<p>
 where $n_ Z \not= 0 \Rightarrow \dim _\delta (Z) = k$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The abelian group of all $k$-cycles on $X$ is denoted $Z_ k(X)$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>